# Checks each standard cell the netlist uses: its Verilog model, as gate.ys reads it,
# against the function the Liberty file gives it (the file the flow synthesised against).
# These are two views of the cell from different sources, and they have to agree for the
# gate model to mean the chip. The Makefile appends one block per cell after these lines.
# equiv_simple steps a flop without looking at which clock edge moves it, so the Liberty
# flops are asserted to take the rising edge here, and the model's flops in gate.ys.

read_liberty -ignore_miss_func cells.lib
design -stash liberty

read_verilog ../netlist_equiv/primitives.v cells.v
hierarchy
proc
flatten
design -stash model
